{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `obs_t_calib`, `obs_t_fall`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: the original likelihood for `obs_t_fall` was written as indexed sampling statements inside nested loops. SafeStan requires a protected observation to be scored exactly once as a plain top-level identifier outside loops, so `obs_t_fall` is represented in `model_safe.stan` as a length `N_drops * N_heights` vector and scored once with a vectorized `normal` statement. `data_safe.json` deterministically flattens the supplied nested `obs_t_fall` array in drop-major order: Stan element `(n - 1) * N_heights + h` is the original `obs_t_fall[n][h]`. The mean vector is filled with the same indexing, preserving the original product likelihood. Priors and generated quantities are otherwise unchanged.
","model_safe_stan":"functions {
  real t_fall(real g, real h) {
    return sqrt(2 * h / g);
  }
}

data {
  // Detector calibration data
  int N_calibrations;
  array[N_calibrations] real obs_t_calib;    // seconds

  // Falling data
  int N_heights;
  array[N_heights] real<lower=0> heights;    // meters
  int N_drops;
  vector[N_drops * N_heights] obs_t_fall;    // seconds, flattened by drop then height
}

parameters {
  real<lower=0> sigma_t; // seconds
  real g;                // meters per second squared
}

model {
  // Prior model
  sigma_t ~ normal(0, 0.5);
  g ~ inv_gamma(1.49, 2.83);

  // Observational model
  obs_t_calib ~ normal(rep_vector(0, N_calibrations), sigma_t);

  {
    vector[N_drops * N_heights] mu_t_fall;

    for (n in 1:N_drops) {
      for (h in 1:N_heights) {
        int i = (n - 1) * N_heights + h;
        mu_t_fall[i] = t_fall(g, heights[h]);
      }
    }

    obs_t_fall ~ normal(mu_t_fall, sigma_t);
  }
}

// Simulate a full observation from each value of the parameters
generated quantities {
  array[N_drops, N_heights] real obs_t_fall_post_pred;

  for (n in 1:N_drops) {
    for (h in 1:N_heights) {
      real mu_t_fall = t_fall(g, heights[h]);
      obs_t_fall_post_pred[n, h] = normal_rng(mu_t_fall, sigma_t);
    }
  }
}
